{"instance_id": "pallets__flask-3193", "repo": "pallets/flask", "base_commit": "3596b1ab61cea85edb8970e83ff61daa073facf8", "issue_url": "https://github.com/pallets/flask/issues/3193", "query": "Flask Session variable not available in threads\nFor example of passing via a Queue that does not work. https://github.com/HourGlss/FlaskSSE/blob/master/sse/sse.py\r\n\r\n### Expected Behavior\r\nSession is a global variable\r\n\r\n### Actual Behavior\r\nWhen passed via a queue the keys and associated values are dropped. When attempting to access globally, no keys are available even if they had been added by endpoints\r\n\r\n### Environment\r\n\r\n* Python version: 3.7\r\n* Flask version: Default install\r\n* Werkzeug version: Default install", "pr_urls": ["https://github.com/pallets/flask/pull/6133"], "weak_targets": ["tests/test_basic.py/test_method_route"], "weak_source_targets": [], "modified_test_functions": ["tests/test_basic.py/test_method_route"], "review_flags": ["low_identifier_overlap"], "candidate_evaluations": [], "groundtruth_status": "unverified_multi_target_candidates"}
